\par Here is how that "1 by 1" process looks inside the CPU hardware:
\par 
\par 1. The Clock Beat
\par The CPU has a "metronome" called the System Clock (that\rquote s the GHz number you see when you buy a laptop). Every time the clock ticks, the CPU can perform one tiny part of an instruction.
\par 
\par Tick 1: Move data from RAM to Register A.
\par 
\par Tick 2: Move data from RAM to Register B.
\par 
\par Tick 3: The function triggers the math circuit. Register C changes its value to the result.
\par 
\par Tick 4: Move the value from Register C back to RAM.
